<section class="bhd-page__feature"><div><p class="bhd-page__kicker">The company thesis</p><h2>Build value where product, evidence and access reinforce each other</h2><p>Best Hydrate's opportunity is broader than a single flavour or sales channel, but the public investor story should stay anchored to what exists today. The company has a commercial hydration product, an expanding public science architecture, external research activity and a brand being developed across performance, daily hydration, medical-development and humanitarian contexts.</p><p>The investment case is therefore a platform thesis with staged proof points, not a claim that every future application is already validated or commercialized.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__split"><div class="bhd-page__split-media"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/6285077/pexels-photo-6285077.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Business professionals reviewing charts and documents at a table" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="bhd-page__split-copy"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">What is public today</p><h2>Separate current assets from future ambition</h2><ul><li>Best Hydrate Inc., an Alberta corporation founded in 2021</li><li>A current Canadian consumer hydration product and public commerce operation</li><li>Natural Product Number 80118664 identified on current product materials</li><li>A 2026 Frontiers in Nutrition review with Best Hydrate Inc. author affiliation</li><li>A Canadian Best Hydrate design-mark application listed by CIPO</li><li>Public research, partnership and clinical-development architecture that distinguishes status and evidence levels</li></ul><p>Private financial information, capitalization, forecasts and financing terms are not published on this page and should be reviewed directly with qualified prospective investors.</p></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Value-building tracks</p><h2>Four areas investors can evaluate separately</h2><div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4"><article><h3>Consumer product</h3><p>Product-market fit, repeat purchase, channel economics, customer education and brand development.</p></article><article><h3>Research</h3><p>Publications, collaborations, pilot studies and progressively stronger evidence around hydration questions.</p></article><article><h3>Channel expansion</h3><p>Retail, distribution and partnership growth where operational and customer fit are demonstrated.</p></article><article><h3>Future applications</h3><p>Clinical-development and humanitarian work that must earn appropriate evidence, regulatory and implementation pathways.</p></article></div></section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid"><article class="bhd-page__prose"><p class="bhd-page__kicker">Investor materials</p><h2>Detailed diligence belongs in a direct process</h2><p>Qualified investors may request appropriate corporate documents, capitalization information, historical financials, projections, financing objectives, use-of-funds plans and other diligence materials directly from the company. The public website is not intended to substitute for those materials or for professional legal, accounting or investment advice.</p><p>Forward-looking plans can change materially as research, regulation, commercial results, financing and partnerships evolve.</p></article><aside class="bhd-page__callout"><span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Investor standard</span><h3>Public facts are not a forecast.</h3><p>Pipeline opportunities, research programs and strategic plans should be evaluated for uncertainty as well as upside.</p></aside></section>

